cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite HP-GSBS and the original GSBS papers."
title: "HP-GSBS: High-Performance Greedy State Boundary Search"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Yanzhe"
    family-names: "Zhao"
    affiliation: "Tianjin University"
version: "0.2.0.dev0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/JustinZHAO-05/HP-GSBS"
url: "https://github.com/JustinZHAO-05/HP-GSBS/tree/feat/v0.2-streaming-moments-gpu-optimization"
abstract: >-
  HP-GSBS is a high-performance implementation of Greedy State Boundary
  Search for multivariate neural time series, with CPU, PyTorch CUDA, and
  Triton CUDA routes. The release includes synthetic examples, tests,
  benchmarks, and reports of agreement with statesegmentation 0.0.6 within
  the documented validation domain. FP64 is the scientific default; FP32
  remains experimental. Private EEG inputs are not redistributed.
keywords:
  - neuroscience
  - neural time series
  - EEG
  - event segmentation
  - Greedy State Boundary Search
  - scientific software
